[Music]  as a freshman stepping on campus in the  year 2000  i was just a lost little puppy i wasn't  a good student  quite frankly i wasn't a good person so  i actually think that's  a big part of the reason why i connect  with some of the students here is  because  i let them in to the imperfection  um okay a first really  physical difference would be that  freshman year i came here and had blue  hair  wow that was so long ago so i met andrew  lohmann  in western heritage when i had blue hair  and we are getting married about a month  after we graduate in may  one of the key ways that my relationship  with andrew has helped me  grow is really just actively practicing  or growing in  selflessness especially in college in  general where it's very easy to focus  inward and to be this is what i need or  this is how much i need to study  just kind of realizing that it's less  the grade that you get and more the  conversation or  the knowledge you gain or the people you  meet along the way  i had kind of viewed myself as you know  like a mediocre student  but a number of different faculty  members showed confidence in me and said  hey it doesn't really matter where  you've been it matters where you're  going to go  so dr wolfram gives out swords for the  best grade in a class and i got the best  grade in both those classes and he gave  me a sword that he bought from the local  county fair  having a professor show confidence in me  that i didn't have for myself  was this really moving thing that pushed  me to actually do what i became  that relational side of things here is  so essential to the hillsdale experience  and getting to talk about these things  from augustine's confessions to boe  boethius's consolation  philosophy to platonic dialogues like  all these things  that four years ago or three years ago  my freshman self never would have really  imagined  that's i think the most vital or the  most important  the most uniquely hillsdale about all of  it  but that's 